` FINK ATLAS "sprites", made by Fink from sample.fink. Do not change this file: change the art
` in Fink and export again (Ctrl+E). List this file FIRST in the game's FadeSource items: the constants
` are text replacement, so they have to come before anything that uses them.
`
`   atlas = fink_load_sprites()     loads it, once, at the start
`   play fink sprite spr, TAG_HERO_WALK     plays a clip on a sprite
`   set fink sprite palette spr, PAL_RED    swaps its colors

#constant FINK_SPRITES_STAMP 699883405

` clips: TAG_<ASSET> is an asset's whole timeline, TAG_<ASSET>_<TAG> one of its tags
#constant TAG_SLIME 2
#constant TAG_SLIME_IDLE 5
#constant TAG_SLIME_HOP 6
#constant TAG_COIN 10
#constant TAG_COIN_SPIN 11

` points: fink sprite point x(spr, POINT_HERO_HAND) / y() say where one is on screen
#constant POINT_SLIME_TOP 8

` data maps: fink atlas map(atlas, MAP_NORMAL) is the map's texture id, for set effect param texture
#constant MAP_LIGHT 0

` palette rows: which colors a sprite is drawn with
#constant PAL_BASE 0
#constant PAL_RED 1

FUNCTION fink_load_sprites()
    atlasId = fink atlas load("Textures/sprites", FINK_SPRITES_STAMP)
ENDFUNCTION atlasId
